run's T22, Risk 40, chose null: "`extracted_answer` describes something pulled out of the
generated response; neither new mode extracts anything from it, and Part 2 introduces
`judge_score` precisely because the judge's value needed a home", and named the tests' reading as
the likely alternative: "An author whose evaluator returns a uniform `(passed, extracted)` pair
would naturally leak the judge's extracted string into `extracted_answer`".

